// Practice quiz: Web-layer tests with MockMvc
// Minimum release, November 2026: author-checked, no independent review. Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: spring-boot/validation-errors-and-testing/web-layer-tests-with-mockmvc

::o1 slice::Which annotation runs a test against the MVC layer without services or repositories? {
=@WebMvcTest#Correct. It loads the web slice for a controller.
~@SpringBootTest#Not quite. That loads the whole app.
~@DataJpaTest#Not quite. That loads the persistence slice.
~@Entity#Not quite. That is not a test annotation.
}

::o1 no network::How does MockMvc reach a controller? {
~Through a real socket on port 8080#Not quite. It does not use a socket.
=It calls the MVC layer directly with no network#Correct. No real server is needed.
~Through the database#Not quite. The database is not involved.
~Through a browser#Not quite. No browser is used.
}

::o2 error path::How do you test a 404 path in @WebMvcTest without a database? {
=A fake or mock service that signals not found#Correct. The slice needs only the collaborator behavior.
~Delete the controller#Not quite. That would test nothing.
~Point at a production database#Not quite. Never do that for this.
~Assert only 200#Not quite. That skips the error path.
}

::o3 reading status failure::A test reports Status expected 200 but was 404. Where do you look first? {
~The JSON field names#Not quite. That concerns a body, once the status is right.
~The JVM version#Not quite. That is unlikely.
=The mapping path and any handler returning 404#Correct. The status says no resource or route answered as expected.
~Maven settings#Not quite. That is unlikely.
}

::o3 reading value failure::A test reports that the JSON value at a path differs from what was expected. What does this suggest? {
~The path was never matched#Not quite. It would likely show a status failure.
~The server did not start#Not quite. A test result exists.
~Security blocked it#Not quite. That shows up as a status.
=The request worked, and the data or mapping differs#Correct. The status passed, so look at the payload.
}

